---
title: "Sanitation and Safety"
code: "HRI-158"
category: "hospitality-restaurant-institutional-management"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Covers the moral and legal responsibilities of management to ensure a sanitary and safe environment in a food service operation. Emphasizes the causes and prevention of foodborne illnesses in conformity with federal, state and local guidelines. Focuses on OSHA standards in assuring safe working conditions. Lecture 3 hours.
